condition_name: Adenoid Diseases
condition_slug: adenoid-diseases
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A syndrome due to hyperplasia/hypertrophy of the adenoid tissue in the nasopharynx. Commoner in children aged 2 - 6 years.
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features of Adenoid Diseases
    features[6]: Nasal obstruction and mouth-breathing,Snoring at night,Obstructive sleep apnoea,Progressive deafness due to secretory otitis media,Chronic infection of adenoid tissue may be present,Symptom may subside spontaneously as adenoid regress and become atrophic with age
investigations[3]: X-ray of nasopharynx,X-ray of sinuses and chest,Nasal endoscopy
treatment:
  goals[2]: To improve nasopharyngeal airway and nasal breathing,To treat concurrent infection
  non_drug[1]: Adenoidectomy in severe cases
  drug[3]: "Decongestants: Psuedoephedrine syrup (6-12 years: 30 mg (5 mL of syrup) orally 8 hourly; 2-5 years: 15 mg (2.5 mL) 4-8 hourly)","Ephedrine nasal drops (0.5%): Instill into nostrils twice daily and at night time","Antibiotics: Amoxicillin syrup 125 - 250 mg orally 8 hourly for 5-7 days"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[3]: Allergic rhinitis,Sinusitis,Otitis media
complications[3]: Sinusitis,Recurrent otitis media,Pneumonitis
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null